                <pb facs="0479" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v12/pg439"/>

                <head>184. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On January 7, the White House announced that President Eisenhower had appointed
                    James P. Richards as Special Assistant to the President with the personal rank
                    of Ambassador to advise and assist the President and the Secretary of State on
                    problems of the Middle Eastern area. In particular, Richards was commissioned to
                    head a special group of Department of State, Department of Defense, and
                    International Cooperation Administration officials to implement certain aspects
                    of U.S. Middle Eastern policies. For text of the announcement, see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, January 28, 1957, page 130.</p>
            </div>
